{"id": "x0151", "pool": "easy-chat", "n_q_chunks": 2, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "In Australia, the main body that regulates banks is called the Australian Sa fety and Investment Commission, or ASIC for short. They make sure banks follow rules about how they operate, protect customers' money, and act fairly. They also work with other groups like the Reserve Bank of Australia, which helps manage the economy. So AS IC plays a big role in keeping the banking system safe and reliable.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 22, "carrier_ended": null}
