{"id": "x0167", "pool": "easy-chat", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "That's a great idea. Rearing chickens can be a fun and rewarding experience, especially if you enjoy gardening or outdoor activities. Chick ens are relatively easy to care for, provided you have the space and resources to provide them with shelter, food and protection from predator s. You'll need a safe coop where they can rest at night, along with a run for them to explore during the day. They eat mostly seeds, grain s, insects and kitchen scraps, so it can actually save money over time. Plus, you'll get fresh eggs regularly. Just make sure you check local regulations first, as some areas have rules about keeping livestock. If you decide to go ahead, starting with just a few birds is usually the best approach to learn the ropes without getting overwhelmed.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 30, "carrier_ended": null}
