{"id": "x0231", "pool": "easy-chat", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "If you're looking to fly fish for trout in Washington State, the Skagit River near Mount Rainier is an excellent spot. It' s known for its clear water and abundant tro ut, especially during the spring run off. Another great location is the Wen chlanda Creek, which offers a more intimate fishing experience with plenty of natural pools perfect for dry fly fishing. Don't forget to check local regulations before heading out!", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 19, "carrier_ended": null}
