{"id": "x0279", "pool": "easy-chat", "n_q_chunks": 2, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The first person to record the weather was probably a farmer or herder who noticed that the weather affected their crops or animals. They might have kept track of rain fall, sun shine, and season s just by watching what happened around them. Over time, people started writing down these observations, like in old calendar s or journal s. So while there wasn't a single person who invented weather recording, early human s were definitely among the first to notice and remember how the weather changed things.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 28, "carrier_ended": null}
