{"id": "x0695", "pool": "know-open", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "It's about 0. 1 millimeters, or 1 00 micrometers.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 5, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0703", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 7, "onset_chunk": 6, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "When a dog sees a cat, the message travels from its eyes to its brain. So the correct answer is option A, brain. The dog ’s eyes detect the cat and send signals to the brain, which processes what it sees.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 12, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0711", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 13, "onset_chunk": 12, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is D. Only plant cells can perform photosyn thesis. Plant cells have structures called chloroplasts that allow them to convert sunlight into energy, which animal cells do not possess.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 13, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0719", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 27, "onset_chunk": 26, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "So, the correct statement is D. The molecules in ice are less free to move than the molecules in liquid water. Now let me explain why this is true and why the other options aren't correct. First, both ice and liquid water are made of the same molecules— H2O, or water molecule s. So option B is wrong because the atoms don' t change when water freeze s. Next, temperature affects energy. Ice forms at a lower temperature than liquid water, so the molecule s in ice actually have less energy than those in liquid water. That means option A is incorrect too. As for electric charge, the water molecule s stay the same in both states, so they don' t gain or lose charge just by changing state. So option C isn't right either. Finally, in ice, the water molecule s are locked into a rigid structure due to hydrogen bonds, which restrict s their movement. In liquid water, these bond s break and reform quickly, allowing the molecule s to flow more freely. This is why ice melt s to become liquid water—it gains energy and the molecules can move around more easily. So yes, the molecules in ice are definitely less free to move than those in liquid water.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 59, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0727", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 20, "onset_chunk": 20, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "So we know that X scratch es Y, and then Y scratch es Z. That means X is harder than Y, and Y is harder than Z. And then Z scratch es W. That means Z is harder than W. So if you put all of those together in order from hard est to soft est, it's going to be X, Y, Z, and then W. So W is the softest one of the four. The answer is A.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 23, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0735", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 16, "onset_chunk": 15, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Heat moves from her hand to the ice cube. So the correct answer is A. He at moves from her hand to the ice cube. When Anna holds the ice cube, her body heat transfers to the ice, causing it to melt.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 12, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0743", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 14, "onset_chunk": 13, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The most common reasons for animal migration are changes in season and food availability. So animals often move to find better feeding grounds, especially during different seasons when resources change. This makes option B the best answer.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 15, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0751", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The moon passes in front of the sun once per day.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 3, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0759", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 18, "onset_chunk": 17, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The radiant energy that comes to Earth from the sun is a range of many wavelengths, from long to very short. So it' s not just one wave length or even just visible light; it includes a broad spectrum covering infrared, visible, and ultraviolet wavelengths. This wide range is why some of the energy becomes heat while other parts are visible light.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 19, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0767", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 12, "onset_chunk": 11, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Cars are powered by gasoline made from oil, which is the best way to conserve gasoline? A. Car pool to school. B. Ride a bus to school. C. Ride a bike to school. D. Drive alone to school. The answer is C. R ide a bike to school.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 14, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0775", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 14, "onset_chunk": 14, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Approximately 71 percent of the Earth's surface is covered with water. The majority of this is salt water and is found in the oceans. Where is the majority of the Earth' s fresh water found? A ice, B lakes, C rivers, D the atmosphere? I' ll tell you right now, it's A ice.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 16, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0783", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 7, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The nutrient source for some fungi is dead organisms. Fungi play a key role in de composing organic material from plants and animals, breaking it down into simpler substances that can be reused by other living things. So while they may use oxygen and carbon dioxide during their metabolic processes, the actual nutrients they get come from dec eased matter.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 21, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0791", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 13, "onset_chunk": 12, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The nucleus of the cell control s its activities by directing genetic information, much like a command center. In humans, the body system that performs a similar function is the central nervous system. It processes information and coordinates responses throughout the body. So the correct answer is B, the central nervous system.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 21, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0799", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 22, "onset_chunk": 21, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "I'd go with D, a model of a stream flowing down a hillside. That would show how water moves and carves the land over time. The other options focus more on rain fall or fog, which are less about shaping the ground itself.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 13, "carrier_ended": null}
